  <!-- ============ ABOUT ============ -->
  <section class="about" id="about">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow reveal-up">Act I — Background</span>
      <div class="about-grid">
        <div class="about-copy reveal-up">
          <p>I design like someone who has had to <strong>build the edge cases</strong>, not only present the happy path.</p>
          <p class="about-support">I studied Computer Science at Vellore Institute of Technology, Vellore from 2021 to 2025, then joined MyGate full time as an Associate Software Developer in July 2025. A year of shipping production interfaces changed what I paid attention to—not just whether a screen worked, but why a flow was structured that way, where users hesitated, and what happened outside the happy path. By July 2026, that curiosity had become the direction I wanted to pursue: UI/UX and product design.</p>

          <div class="history">
            <div class="history-row"><time>Now</time><h4>Product &amp; UX design</h4></div>
            <div class="history-row"><time>Jul 2025–Jul 2026</time><h4>Associate Software Developer · MyGate</h4></div>
            <div class="history-row"><time>2021–2025</time><h4>BTech, Computer Science · VIT Vellore</h4></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="identity-stage reveal-up" id="portrait" aria-label="Three perspectives shaping my work">
          <div class="identity-core"><strong>A.</strong><span>Product perspective</span></div>
          <article class="identity-card engineer"><small>01 · Engineer</small><h3>Can it survive reality?</h3><p>States, constraints, hand-off, and what happens when the ideal flow breaks.</p></article>
          <article class="identity-card designer"><small>02 · Designer</small><h3>Can it feel obvious?</h3><p>Hierarchy, interaction, and reducing the translation users must do.</p></article>
          <article class="identity-card performer"><small>03 · Performer</small><h3>Where is attention now?</h3><p>Timing, anticipation, feedback, and the half-second before an action.</p></article>
          
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

