  <!-- ============ THINKING SYSTEM ============ -->
  <section class="craft" id="craft">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow reveal-up">Act III — Approach</span>
      <div class="craft-head reveal-up">
        <h2>How I think before I design.</h2>
        <p>The same sequence kept showing up across all three projects.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="mobile-thinking-process" id="mobileThinkingProcess" aria-label="My four-step thinking process">
        <div class="mobile-thinking-list">
          <article class="mobile-thinking-step" data-step="01">
        <span class="mobile-thinking-label">Observe behaviour</span>
        <h3>Where is the product fighting the user?</h3>
        <p>I start with what people naturally do, not what the interface expects them to do.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="mobile-thinking-step" data-step="02">
        <span class="mobile-thinking-label">Define the friction</span>
        <h3>What is actually causing it?</h3>
        <p>I keep digging until the visible problem becomes one clear reason worth designing around.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="mobile-thinking-step" data-step="03">
        <span class="mobile-thinking-label">Make one product decision</span>
        <h3>What is the smallest move that changes behaviour?</h3>
        <p>I would rather change the product model than add another screen, setting, or feature.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="mobile-thinking-step" data-step="04">
        <span class="mobile-thinking-label">Own the trade-off</span>
        <h3>If this gets better, what gets harder?</h3>
        <p>Every decision has a cost. I choose where that cost belongs instead of pretending it disappears.</p>
      </article>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="thinking-scroll" id="thinkingScroll">
        <div class="thinking-sticky">
          <div class="thinking-stage">
            <article class="thinking-card is-scroll-card" id="thinkingCard" data-step-glyph="01" aria-live="polite">
              <div class="thinking-copy">
                <div class="thinking-copy-top">
                  <span class="step-no" id="thinkingStepLabel">Observe behaviour</span>
                </div>
                <h3 id="thinkingStepTitle">Where is the product fighting the user?</h3>
                <p id="thinkingStepText">I start with what people naturally do, not what the interface expects them to do.</p>
                <div class="thinking-progress" id="thinkingProgress" aria-hidden="true">
                  <i class="is-active"></i><i></i><i></i><i></i>
                </div>
              </div>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>




  
